    "notes": "Reviewed catalog/state/autoDepot/scene/selection and existing direct tests. Four Items now own identity, dimensions and model metadata. The shared state factory consumes those defaults; automatic depot consumes the catalog projection. Type behavior is retained; model-name trash compatibility routing removed. Their existing BOM policy remains decision-required with null source: no unit, recipe, resolver, Raw BOM or Final BOM policy was introduced. F-014 is reviewedNotAffected; F-019 is affected only for these four products and is not globally closed. Other discovered findings retain existing ownership and behavior. User explicitly waived old-project compatibility: no aliases or legacy migration. Broad main/scene path domains include assets and performance even though no asset bytes change. Build and all 610 unit/integration tests passed after the BOM-scope correction. Existing source-text tests normalize CRLF before matching, and the door filename assertion checks exact directory-entry casing so Windows case-insensitive lookup does not report the canonical lowercase file as a legacy uppercase file. Playwright and Chromium are installed. The full 20-test Chromium suite passed before the BOM-scope correction, including four canonical catalog drag checks, automatic-depot save/open persistence, mini-fridge dimensions, and all plastic-trash-bin catalog/model/persistence/depot checks; the correction only restores the pre-existing non-browser BOM policy. Remote CI remains unverified."
  },
